window.MR.strategy={"_meta":{"captured":"2026-09-02","what_this_is":"What a unit has to cost to win each kind of buyer, and which counterparties have a structural reason to buy. Every number restates a cited row on the Costs or Deals tabs; rows marked derived are arithmetic on those inputs with the formula printed.","method":"Built 2026-09-02 from the site's own benchmarks, cost bands, tracker and site records, with the fixed-staffing inputs read from Idaho National Laboratory's cached cost reports. No new sources were fetched; the open questions each row ends with are the next research pass.","derived_note":"Derived figures are conversions of cited inputs at stated assumptions, not estimates of what any reactor will cost. Change the assumption and the number moves; the formula is printed so a reader can.","advantage_types":[{"id":"nuclear-interest","label":"Has already signed or declared for nuclear","gloss":"A signed instrument, a letter of intent or a consortium membership naming nuclear."},{"id":"off-grid-diesel","label":"Off-grid, burning diesel or fuel oil","gloss":"The incumbent is delivered fuel, so the price to beat is $250/MWh and up."},{"id":"vendor-gap","label":"A funded buyer whose vendor withdrew","gloss":"Feasibility done, money or a licence track in place, and no reactor company on the other side of the table."},{"id":"wires-constraint","label":"Waiting on transmission or distribution","gloss":"The load exists or is funded and the wire to serve it does not."},{"id":"speed-or-land","label":"Needs power before the grid can deliver it","gloss":"Delivery date is the product; land is offered or already held."},{"id":"sovereignty","label":"Energy sovereignty is the stated goal","gloss":"A tribal, territorial or national owner for whom control of supply is the point, not only cost."},{"id":"co-location","label":"Builds the load and the generation together","gloss":"Generation sized to one owner's load on one site, so nothing is sold across a fence."},{"id":"supply-chain","label":"Holds a chokepoint the whole class depends on","gloss":"Fuel fabrication and enrichment: a partner that can hold up every vendor's schedule."}],"status_values":["signed","selected","letter-of-intent","consortium","orphaned","evidence-only","policy-gated"],"extra_sectors":["Defense installations","Supply chain"],"extra_sectors_note":"Sectors the Applications taxonomy does not carry, declared here so a prospect's sector is always a named value: defence procurement is its own buyer frame, and the fuel partners sell to vendors rather than buy power."},"ladder":{"question":"What does a unit have to cost to win each buyer?","note":"Four rungs, each a published cost scenario with the buyers it opens. The published capital-cost estimates disagree by about five times, so a price quoted without its rung says nothing.","rungs":[{"id":"first-unit","name":"First unit","scenario":"One well-executed first unit, costed bottom-up by Idaho National Laboratory","capex_low_kwe":14500,"capex_high_kwe":22000,"lcoe_low_mwh":325,"lcoe_high_mwh":325,"lcoe_note":"INL's first-unit point estimate. NEI's first-of-a-kind band for the same class runs $140–410/MWh.","opens":["arctic-communities","island-bases","remote-mines"],"opens_note":"Rural Alaska and Nunavut at any published estimate; island bases where the gas alternative already costs $18,000/kW plus shipped fuel; the upper half of the remote-mine diesel band only.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf"},{"label":"NEI — Cost Competitiveness of Micro-Reactors for Remote Markets (2019)","url":"https://www.nei.org/resources/reports-briefs/cost-competitiveness-micro-reactors-remote-markets"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_N3943019F9909 (PIID N3943019F9909), Siemens Government Technologies","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_N3943019F9909_9700_DEAM3609GO29041_8900/"}]},{"id":"mass-produced","name":"Mass-produced","scenario":"An assembly line building ten units a year, same design","capex_low_kwe":6000,"capex_high_kwe":6000,"lcoe_low_mwh":120,"lcoe_high_mwh":150,"lcoe_note":"INL's mass-produced case. NEI's nth-of-a-kind band for the class runs $90–330/MWh.","opens":["remote-mines","critical-facilities","federal-firm-generation"],"opens_note":"The whole remote-diesel band; the $150/MWh healthcare price behind the meter; firm on-site generation at grid-connected bases, where the federal price stamp is $5,400/kW installed.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf"},{"label":"NEI — Cost Competitiveness of Micro-Reactors for Remote Markets (2019)","url":"https://www.nei.org/resources/reports-briefs/cost-competitiveness-micro-reactors-remote-markets"},{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge — University Healthcare Clinic Powers Up Microgrid with On-Site Solar and Tesla Battery in California","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/microgrids/critical-services/news/55312608/university-healthcare-clinic-powers-up-microgrid-with-on-site-solar-and-tesla-battery-in-california"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_W912HN26CA001 (PIID W912HN26CA001), David Boland Inc.","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_W912HN26CA001_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"}]},{"id":"optimized","name":"Optimized design, modeled","scenario":"The capital costs the University of Michigan optimization was allowed to draw from; inputs, not observed costs","capex_low_kwe":2515,"capex_high_kwe":3970,"lcoe_low_mwh":48,"lcoe_high_mwh":78,"lcoe_note":"With the production tax credit. The paper reports the credit cutting LCOE by 22–24%, so the unsubsidised figure lands near $63–103/MWh.","opens":["data-centers","process-heat","ports"],"opens_note":"Grid-adjacent buyers: data centers against colocation and the grid tariff, factories against a special-contract tariff, ports against a distribution upgrade. Each also needs a schedule or resilience reason to pay above the grid.","sources":[{"label":"Abdussami, Khaleb, Gao & Verma (Univ. of Michigan) — Evaluation of Nuclear Microreactor Cost-competitiveness in Current Electricity Markets Considering Reactor Cost Uncertainties (arXiv:2506.13361)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.13361"},{"label":"Abdussami et al., Nuclear Engineering and Design (arXiv 2506.13361)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13361"}]},{"id":"out-of-reach","name":"Below every published estimate","scenario":"Incumbents priced under $3,000/kW installed, where no microreactor study lands","capex_low_kwe":1420,"capex_high_kwe":2800,"lcoe_low_mwh":null,"lcoe_high_mwh":null,"lcoe_note":"A greenhouse operator built 13 MW of gas engines at about $1,420/kW on a four-year payback; a university's 50-year concession bought gas CHP at about $2,800/kW; a battery plant buys energy at $24.56/MWh plus a redacted demand charge.","opens":[],"opens_note":"Nothing at 1–20 MW. These buyers pay grid or gas prices and have no resilience or logistics premium to spend.","sources":[{"label":"DOE CHP Technical Assistance Partnership (ORNL) - Houweling's Tomatoes project profile","url":"https://chptap.ornl.gov/profile/101/houweling-tomatoes.pdf"},{"label":"The Ohio State University, Business and Finance — Energy Concession Agreement","url":"https://busfin.osu.edu/university-business/comprehensive-energy-management/energy-concession-agreement"},{"label":"Kentucky Public Service Commission - Special Contract for Electric Service between Kentucky Utilities Company and BlueOval SK, LLC (Case No. 2023-00123)","url":"https://psc.ky.gov/pscecf/2023-00123/mike.hornung@lge-ku.com/04142023102139/07_-_KU-BOSK_Special_Contract_-_Contract_FINAL_-_REDACTED.pdf"}]}],"units":{"question":"What is that per unit?","formula":"unit cost = $/kWe × MWe × 1,000","note":"Derived from the rungs above at the unit sizes in the field: the 1 MWe class (Antares, Radiant), the 2.5 MWe heat-pipe archetype, INL's 6 MWe reference and the 20 MWe top of the band (BWXT). The Army has warned that dividing a Janus award by its unit count does not give a unit price, because the award also pays for development; these are the study figures, not award arithmetic.","sizes_mwe":[1,2.5,6,20],"rows":[{"rung":"first-unit","usd_millions":{"1":[14.5,22.0],"2.5":[36.2,55.0],"6":[87.0,132.0],"20":[290.0,440.0]}},{"rung":"mass-produced","usd_millions":{"1":[6.0,6.0],"2.5":[15.0,15.0],"6":[36.0,36.0],"20":[120.0,120.0]}},{"rung":"optimized","usd_millions":{"1":[2.5,4.0],"2.5":[6.3,9.9],"6":[15.1,23.8],"20":[50.3,79.4]}}],"sources":[{"label":"POWER — U.S. Army Mobilizes $2.2B Janus Program to Deploy More Than 20 Commercial Microreactors","url":"https://www.powermag.com/u-s-army-mobilizes-2-2b-janus-program-to-deploy-more-than-20-commercial-microreactors/","quote":"One thing you definitely cannot do is divide the dollars by the number of reactors"},{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — A Bottom-Up Cost Estimation Tool for Nuclear Microreactors (INL/RPT-25-87273, Sept 2025)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/09/2025-Document-INL-RPT-25-87273.pdf"},{"label":"ANS — Reactor Pilot Program status at the July 4 deadline (Mark-0 criticality)","url":"https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-02/article-8178/the-deadline-arrives-checking-in-on-the-reactor-pilot-program/"},{"label":"Radiant — Series D announcement","url":"https://www.radiantnuclear.com/blog/series-d-announcement/"}]},"conversion":{"question":"How much price does each $1,000/kWe cost?","formula":"$/MWh per $1,000/kWe = 1,000 × CRF ÷ (8.76 × capacity factor); CRF = r(1+r)^n ÷ ((1+r)^n − 1)","note":"A rule of thumb for reading the segments below: at a 5% real discount rate over 20 years and a 95% capacity factor, every $1,000/kWe of capital adds about $10/MWh to the price. Over 40 years it is about $7. The rate and the 20-year life are the University of Michigan study's; the 95% capacity factor is INL's and NEI's. It is a conversion, not a cost estimate, and it leaves out fuel, staff and financing during construction.","rows":[{"life_years":20,"real_rate":0.05,"cf":0.95,"crf":0.0802,"usd_per_mwh_per_1000_kwe":9.6},{"life_years":40,"real_rate":0.05,"cf":0.95,"crf":0.0583,"usd_per_mwh_per_1000_kwe":7.0}],"sources":[{"label":"Abdussami, Khaleb, Gao & Verma (Univ. of Michigan) — Evaluation of Nuclear Microreactor Cost-competitiveness in Current Electricity Markets Considering Reactor Cost Uncertainties (arXiv:2506.13361)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.13361","quote":"Real discount rate 5%"},{"label":"Abdussami, Khaleb, Gao & Verma (Univ. of Michigan) — Evaluation of Nuclear Microreactor Cost-competitiveness in Current Electricity Markets Considering Reactor Cost Uncertainties (arXiv:2506.13361)","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.13361","quote":"Reactor lifetime 20 years"},{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf","quote":"The estimated capacity factor is around 95%"},{"label":"NEI — Cost Competitiveness of Micro-Reactors for Remote Markets (2019)","url":"https://www.nei.org/resources/reports-briefs/cost-competitiveness-micro-reactors-remote-markets"}]}},"floor":{"question":"What never gets cheaper, and what does it cost per megawatt-hour?","note":"Staff, security and monitoring cost the same on the twentieth unit as on the first, and they are charged per reactor. Spread over a 1 MWe unit's output they are a large share of the price; over a 20 MWe unit they are small. INL's reference reactor is 6 MWe, so its staffing numbers are printed here at four unit sizes.","formula":"$/MWh = fixed cost per reactor per year ÷ (MWe × 8,760 × capacity factor), at a 95% capacity factor","cf":0.95,"sizes_mwe":[1,2.5,6,20],"inputs":[{"id":"guard-and-monitor","name":"Security guard and remote monitoring only","usd_per_year":490000,"basis":"INL's autonomous-operation case. A guard on site around the clock is 5 full-time staff, shared one guard per two reactors, about $446K a reactor a year; one remote monitor watches 20 reactors, about $44K a reactor a year. Together about $490K a year per reactor, with operators arriving only for a shutdown, an emergency or refuelling.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf","quote":"securing the reactor 24/7 will require 5 FTEs"},{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf","quote":"it is assumed that one person can monitor 20 reactors"}]},{"id":"inl-staff-first-unit","name":"INL's operations and maintenance staff line, first unit","usd_per_year":3915898,"basis":"The annualized O&M staff account INL attaches to its 6 MWe reference reactor, which the report holds fixed as the reactor gets larger.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf","quote":"Assuming that this cost does not significantly change for microreactors with larger capacities"}]},{"id":"inl-staff-mass-produced","name":"The same staff line, mass-produced","usd_per_year":1488041,"basis":"INL's mass-produced case cuts operations and maintenance cost by 62%. Applied to the staff line above.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf","quote":"Similarly, the O&M costs drop by 62% for the NOAK case"}]}],"rows":[{"input":"guard-and-monitor","usd_per_year":490000,"per_mwh":{"1":58.9,"2.5":23.6,"6":9.8,"20":2.9}},{"input":"inl-staff-first-unit","usd_per_year":3915898,"per_mwh":{"1":470.5,"2.5":188.2,"6":78.4,"20":23.5}},{"input":"inl-staff-mass-produced","usd_per_year":1488041,"per_mwh":{"1":178.8,"2.5":71.5,"6":29.8,"20":8.9}}],"reading":"At 1 MWe, INL's first-unit staff line alone is about $470/MWh, above the whole remote-diesel band, and the mass-produced version is still about $180/MWh. Even the leanest case, a shared guard and a remote monitor, is about $59/MWh at 1 MWe against $3 at 20 MWe. So a single 1 MWe unit at a lone site only clears rural-Alaska prices. The 1 MWe class is a fleet product: fifteen units at Fort Benning, three at Fort Bragg and twenty in the Equinix preorder all share guards, monitors and refuelling crews across one site or one owner, and that sharing is what the price depends on.","sources":[{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — Technoeconomic Evaluation of Microreactor Using Detailed Bottom-up Estimate (INL/RPT-24-80433)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/03/2024-Document-INL-RPT-24-80433.pdf"},{"label":"Idaho National Laboratory — A Bottom-Up Cost Estimation Tool for Nuclear Microreactors (INL/RPT-25-87273, Sept 2025)","url":"https://gain.inl.gov/content/uploads/4/2025/09/2025-Document-INL-RPT-25-87273.pdf"},{"label":"Equinix investor release 2025-08-14","url":"https://investor.equinix.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1079/equinix-collaborates-with-leading-alternative-energy"},{"label":"POWER — The Janus Five: 20+ Commercial Nuclear Microreactors, Starting in 2028","url":"https://www.powermag.com/the-janus-five-20-commercial-nuclear-microreactors-starting-in-2028/","status":"snippet-only"}]},"segments":[{"id":"arctic-communities","name":"Rural Alaska and Nunavut community grids","sector":"Electric Utilities","incumbent":"Diesel cost of service certified by the regulator at $410–1,950/MWh across rural Alaska; Nunavut's territorial utility charges $555–1,130/MWh by customer class.","incumbent_low_mwh":410,"incumbent_high_mwh":1950,"price_form":"Utility rate base or a subsidised tariff. Commercial and industrial load in Alaska pays the full unsubsidised cost, so it is the customer to price against.","term":"Rate-based, so no fixed term; the state's PCE program is the settlement mechanism.","clears":"first-unit","verdict":"Every published microreactor estimate beats this incumbent. Price is not the constraint.","blocker":"Load. Single villages draw tens of kilowatts, twenty times too small for a 1 MWe unit; only hub communities like Kotzebue at 19.7 GWh a year, or an aggregated tribal utility, present a load a reactor can serve. Nunavut adds sealift logistics and the absence of a Canadian microreactor licence.","first_deal":"A mid-size hub at $600–1,000/MWh, owned by the utility or a tribal power company inside the rate base, with public capital: the federal government already pays about $5,000/kW for non-diesel capacity in a 170-person village.","benchmark_ids":["alaska-pce-fy2024-base-rate-order","qulliq-nunavut-interim-rates-2025","kokhanok-paradigm-shift-era-microgrid","tanana-chiefs-alaskan-tribal-energy-sovereignty-era"],"sources":[{"label":"Regulatory Commission of Alaska - Letter Order L2300184, FY2024 PCE base rate change","url":"https://pce.akenergyauthority.org/Documents/FY24%20Base%20Rate%20Change%20Final%20L2300184.pdf"},{"label":"Qulliq Energy Corporation - Interim Electricity Rates effective April 1, 2025 (General Rate Application)","url":"https://www.qec.nu.ca/interim-electricity-rates-effective-april-1-2025-general-rate-application"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_DECD0000120 (FAIN DECD0000120), Kokhanok Village, Lake and Peninsula AK","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_DECD0000120_089/"}]},{"id":"island-bases","name":"Isolated and Arctic federal installations","sector":"Defense installations","incumbent":"Island and interior bases run their own plants on shipped or railed fuel. Guantanamo's replacement gas plant cost $368.8M for 20 MW, about $18,440/kW, and the Navy still valued it at $24.6M a year in savings. Alaska Army installations buy heat and power from a 50-year privatised utility running coal and oil.","incumbent_low_mwh":null,"incumbent_high_mwh":null,"price_form":"A 30-year firm-fixed-price power purchase agreement with the owner-operator, contracted by DLA Energy, is the template the Air Force wrote for Eielson. On Army installations in Alaska the buyer is the privatised utility's rate base.","term":"24–30 years on the ESPC and PPA precedents; 50 years on the utility privatisation.","clears":"first-unit","verdict":"On capital cost a first unit competes where the alternative is $18,000/kW plus a fuel chain. The instrument exists and no price has been published under it.","blocker":"The Eielson award follows NRC licensing, and no price has been disclosed. A reactor at 5 MW supplements a 23 MW coal plant rather than replacing it.","first_deal":"Sell into the instrument that already exists: an ESPC task order or the Doyon rate base at Fort Wainwright, where the displaced fuel is the line item the contractor is already pricing.","benchmark_ids":["guantanamo-bay-lng-espc","eielson-afb-oklo-microreactor-noita","doyon-utilities-alaska-utility-privatization","parris-island-espc-microgrid"],"sources":[{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_N3943019F9909 (PIID N3943019F9909), Siemens Government Technologies","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_N3943019F9909_9700_DEAM3609GO29041_8900/"},{"label":"Oklo Inc. - Oklo Selected as Intended Awardee to Provide Clean, Reliable Power to Eielson Air Force Base in Alaska","url":"https://oklo.com/newsroom/news-details/2025/Oklo-Selected-as-Intended-Awardee-to-Provide-Clean-Reliable-Power-to-Eielson-Air-Force-Base-in-Alaska/default.aspx"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_SP060007C8263 (PIID SP0600-07-C-8263), Doyon Utilities LLC, Fort Wainwright AK","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_SP060007C8263_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"}]},{"id":"remote-mines","name":"Off-grid mines and mineral processing","sector":"Mining","incumbent":"Industrial self-generation in the Canadian North at $250–600/MWh, with a tail to $1,200. Natural Resources Canada puts a first-of-a-kind 20 MWe unit for mining at C$200–350M and expects a 20–60% cost advantage over diesel.","incumbent_low_mwh":250,"incumbent_high_mwh":600,"price_form":"Fixed $/kWh below the incumbent diesel cost, developer-owned behind the fence; 15-year terms at Kathleen Valley and Essakane, 16 at Syama. Mid-tier miners also build and own their own plants, so an owned unit has to be sellable too.","term":"15–16 years is normal off-grid; mine life caps it.","clears":"mass-produced","verdict":"INL's first unit at $325/MWh sits inside the band and loses to cheap diesel at the bottom of it. The mass-produced unit at $120–150/MWh beats the whole band.","blocker":"Mine life against payback: Diavik's solar arrived with two years of production left, and Red Dog closes around 2032. Fleet electrification moves a 25 MW mine to 35–40 MW. And the northern operator's stated fear is a grid collapse at minus 40, so the reactor has to prove it firms the microgrid.","first_deal":"A new long-life mine, or a relocatable 20 MWe unit that can move to the next site, sold through the off-grid power contractor that already holds the site contract.","benchmark_ids":["raglan-mine-wind-storage-tugliq-glencore","smr-for-mining-canada-nrcan-20mwe-cost-band","red-dog-mine-solar-teck-nana-tugliq","syama-gold-mine-aggreko-16-year-psa","kathleen-valley-lithium-zenith-95mw-ppa","diavik-wind-farm-and-solar-rio-tinto","copper-mountain-trolley-assist-12mw-load"],"sources":[{"label":"TUGLIQ Energy Co. / ecoENERGY Innovation Initiative - Glencore RAGLAN Mine Renewable Electricity Smart-Grid Pilot Demonstration, Public Completion Report GC 128296","url":"https://tugliq.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/2016-11-11-tugliq-raglan-public-report-en.pdf"},{"label":"Natural Resources Canada - Small Modular Reactors (SMRs) for Mining","url":"https://natural-resources.canada.ca/energy-sources/nuclear-energy-uranium/small-modular-reactors-smrs-mining"},{"label":"ArcticToday - One of Alaska's flagship mines soon could draw energy from the sun","url":"https://www.arctictoday.com/one-of-alaskas-flagship-mines-soon-could-draw-energy-from-the-sun/"},{"label":"Global Mining Review - Aggreko and Resolute sign hybrid power plant contract","url":"https://www.globalminingreview.com/exploration-development/17122019/aggreko-and-resolute-sign-hybrid-power-plant-contract/"},{"label":"Zenith Energy - Liontown Resources signs Power Purchase Agreement with Zenith Energy","url":"https://zenithenergy.com.au/liontown-resources-signs-power-purchase-agreement-ppa-with-zenith-energy-for-the-largest-off-grid-renewable-energy-hybrid-power-station-in-australia/"},{"label":"Nunatsiaq News - Diavik mine's wind-driven power saves $5 million a year in diesel costs","url":"https://nunatsiaq.com/stories/article/65674diavik_mines_wind-driven_power_saves_5_million_in_diesel_costs/"},{"label":"BC Hydro - A net-zero mine? Copper Mountain takes electrifying first step","url":"https://www.bchydro.com/news/conservation/2022/mining-trolley-trucks.html"}]},{"id":"critical-facilities","name":"Hospitals, water utilities and civic anchors","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","incumbent":"A Southern California clinic buys behind-the-meter power at 15 cents/kWh, flat for 30 years, with no host capital; sub-acute care facilities pay 22–25 cents with a 2% escalator. FEMA values avoided outage loss at $67.6M for one hospital campus and $261M for one water utility, against generator projects of $15.1M and $6.5M.","incumbent_low_mwh":150,"incumbent_high_mwh":250,"price_form":"Resilience service plus energy: an energy-services agreement or energy-as-a-service with zero host capital, the diesel fleet retained for the ten-second start that code requires.","term":"20–30 years on the airport, county and clinic precedents; 50 on the Ohio State concession.","clears":"mass-produced","verdict":"The first unit does not beat $150/MWh. The mass-produced band overlaps it, and the FEMA figures say the ceiling for firm power at these sites is far above what a generator costs.","blocker":"No public authority having jurisdiction has accepted a non-diesel source as a hospital's sole emergency supply, and a hospital's whole campus is single-digit megawatts, so the unit is small and the staffing floor bites.","first_deal":"A water utility or medical campus with a FEMA benefit-cost worksheet already on file, sold as reduced diesel runtime and multi-day firmness with the generators kept.","benchmark_ids":["loma-linda-faculty-medical-clinics-ppa","nextnrg-sunnyside-topanga-microgrid-ppas","waterone-johnson-county-fema-generators","erie-county-medical-center-fema-generators","baystate-health-springfield-chp","montgomery-county-md-pshq-mccf-microgrids","pittsburgh-international-airport-microgrid"],"sources":[{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge — University Healthcare Clinic Powers Up Microgrid with On-Site Solar and Tesla Battery in California","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/microgrids/critical-services/news/55312608/university-healthcare-clinic-powers-up-microgrid-with-on-site-solar-and-tesla-battery-in-california"},{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge — Two California Healthcare Facilities Choose Long-Term Microgrid PPAs with New Developer","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/commercial-microgrids/news/55303895/two-california"},{"label":"FEMA OpenFEMA API — Hazard Mitigation Assistance Projects v4, project LPDM-PJ-07-KS-2022-001 (WaterOne, Johnson County KS)","url":"https://www.fema.gov/api/open/v4/HazardMitigationAssistanceProjects?$filter=projectIdentifier%20eq%20%27LPDM-PJ-07-KS-2022-001%27"},{"label":"FEMA OpenFEMA API — Hazard Mitigation Assistance Projects v4, project DR-4480-0059-R (Erie County Medical Center)","url":"https://www.fema.gov/api/open/v4/HazardMitigationAssistanceProjects?$filter=projectIdentifier%20eq%20%27DR-4480-0059-R%27"},{"label":"The Ohio State University, Business and Finance — Energy Concession Agreement","url":"https://busfin.osu.edu/university-business/comprehensive-energy-management/energy-concession-agreement"},{"label":"PR Newswire / Allegheny County Airport Authority — Pittsburgh International Airport Goes Live with First-of-Its-Kind Microgrid","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/pittsburgh-international-airport-goes-live-with-first-of-its-kind-microgrid-powering-entire-facility-with-natural-gas-and-solar-energy-301333349.html"},{"label":"Montgomery County MD Dept. of General Services — Advanced Energy Projects","url":"https://www.montgomerycountymd.gov/department-general-services/dgs-divisions-offices/office-energy-sustainability/advanced-energy-projects"}]},{"id":"federal-firm-generation","name":"Firm on-site generation at grid-connected bases","sector":"Defense installations","incumbent":"The Army's price stamps for islandable on-site generation: $54.3M for 10 MW at Fort Stewart ($5,433/kW installed, fuel and O&M on top); $5.2M for a 1.5 MW diesel-solar-battery block at Camp Buehring ($3,480/kW of firm capacity); $91.1M for about 10 MW of mixed generation at Parris Island.","incumbent_low_mwh":null,"incumbent_high_mwh":null,"price_form":"Design-build awards and ESPC task orders, increasingly signed by the privatised utility that owns the base's wires rather than by the Army.","term":"3 years for a design-build; 25 for an ESPC.","clears":"mass-produced","verdict":"On capital alone a reactor has to land near $5,400/kW; the mass-produced unit is close and the first unit is three to four times over. The argument is the fuel and O&M line the design-build price does not include.","blocker":"The Army's own program says its reactors will not supply all of a base's power; they run alongside the grid as resilience, so the comparison is a microgrid block, the toughest $/kW in the file.","first_deal":"The Janus conversion itself: the Army expects to move to a power purchase agreement after the first year of operation, which makes the privatised utility and DLA Energy the counterparties to prepare for.","benchmark_ids":["fort-stewart-10mw-generation-plant-microgrid","camp-buehring-resilient-power-microgrid","parris-island-espc-microgrid","aberdeen-proving-ground-microgrid-backup-power"],"sources":[{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_W912HN26CA001 (PIID W912HN26CA001), David Boland Inc.","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_W912HN26CA001_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_W912QR26CA007 (PIID W912QR26CA007), AGCO-PS JV","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_W912QR26CA007_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_N3943017F1901 (PIID N3943017F1901), Ameresco Inc., place of performance Parris Island SC","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_N3943017F1901_9700_DEAM3609GO29029_8900/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_W912QR25CA034 (PIID W912QR25CA034), City Light & Power Aberdeen LLC","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_W912QR25CA034_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"},{"label":"POWER — U.S. Army Mobilizes $2.2B Janus Program to Deploy More Than 20 Commercial Microreactors","url":"https://www.powermag.com/u-s-army-mobilizes-2-2b-janus-program-to-deploy-more-than-20-commercial-microreactors/"}]},{"id":"ports","name":"Marine terminals","sector":"Transportation","incumbent":"Ports already spend $7.0M per container berth and $14.7M per cruise berth to electrify a 1–5 MW hotelling load, and the federal Clean Ports program has committed over $1.4B at two ports to convert diesel machinery into electrical load while funding no supply.","incumbent_low_mwh":null,"incumbent_high_mwh":null,"price_form":"Capital avoidance: the distribution upgrade and demand charges the port has not yet priced, plus a resilience budget that paid $12.2M for a 550 kW microgrid at Long Beach.","term":"Grant periods of 4 years; no term power contract in the record.","clears":"optimized","verdict":"No $/MWh price exists to beat. The reactor competes with a feeder upgrade on a congested urban utility, and its problem is duty cycle: a berth only draws power while a ship is alongside.","blocker":"Duty cycle and the absence of any port that has signed for nuclear in the United States. The one port operator that has signed anywhere is DP World at Thames Freeport, under a UK regulator.","first_deal":"A terminal with a year-round base load (reefers, cranes, fleet charging) where shore power is the seasonal add, sold as the supply the Clean Ports award left unfunded.","benchmark_ids":["carb-at-berth-shore-power-capex","port-of-seattle-cruise-shore-power","port-of-los-angeles-epa-clean-ports","port-authority-ny-nj-epa-clean-ports","port-of-long-beach-microgrid-2022"],"sources":[{"label":"California Dept of Finance / CARB - Standardized Regulatory Impact Assessment, Ocean-Going Vessels At Berth (per-berth capex)","url":"https://dof.ca.gov/media/docs/forecasting/economics/major-regulations/major-regulations-table/SRIA_with_Appendices-Proposed_Control_Measure_for_Ocean-Going_Vessels_At_Berth-080119.pdf"},{"label":"Port of Seattle - The Past, Present, and Future of Shore Power","url":"https://www.portseattle.org/blog/past-present-and-future-shore-power"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_97T27601 (FAIN 97T27601), City of Los Angeles, Clean Ports Program","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_97T27601_068/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_96275025 (FAIN 96275025), Port Authority of New York & New Jersey, Clean Ports Program","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_96275025_068/"},{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge - Port of Long Beach, Schneider Electric start construction on $12.2 million microgrid project","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/google-news-feed/article/11427396/port-of-long-beach-schneider-electric-start-construction-on-122-million-microgrid-project"},{"label":"The Civil Engineer — UK/US partnership fast-tracks SMRs and microreactors (Last Energy PWR-20 / Thames Freeport)","url":"https://www.thecivilengineer.org/news/fast-track-nuclear-how-the-ukus-partnership-accelerates-smrs-and-microreactors"}]},{"id":"data-centers","name":"Data centers and speed-constrained large loads","sector":"Compute","incumbent":"Wholesale colocation asks $196.25 per kW a month, about $269/MWh drawn continuously, for firm delivered power with space and interconnection; PJM capacity clears at $333.44/MW-day, about $121,700 per MW-year before energy. Georgia now requires a 15-year minimum term from any 100 MW load and Virginia bills 85% of contracted demand whether or not it is used.","incumbent_low_mwh":null,"incumbent_high_mwh":269,"price_form":"A long-term capacity and energy agreement, fleet-shaped: Equinix's 20-unit preorder with deposits, Google's fleet agreement against a vendor roadmap, Meta's prepayment. The 1–20 MW sale inside a campus is a dedicated resilience block, priced against colocation and the diesel fleet, not against the grid tariff.","term":"15 years is the regulator's floor in Georgia; 20 years on the signed nuclear PPAs.","clears":"optimized","verdict":"Against grid power only the optimized design with the tax credit competes, and that is a forecast. Against colocation's all-in $269/MWh or a curtailable Texas connection, the mass-produced unit is in range for a dedicated block.","blocker":"Speed. A hyperscaler in Memphis put unpermitted gas turbines in rather than wait for a utility, and even the permitted fallback beat any licensing path. The buyer compares delivery dates first and prices second.","first_deal":"A colocation operator's 1–20 MW resilience block under a fleet preorder, at a site under ERCOT's 10 MW small-generation threshold or in a state that permits behind-the-meter sale, with delivery in 2028–2030 written as the product.","benchmark_ids":["cbre-wholesale-colocation-pricing-h2-2025","pjm-2027-2028-capacity-auction-data-center-driven-price","georgia-power-large-load-tariff-100mw","dominion-virginia-gs5-data-center-rate-class","ercot-sb6-large-load-interconnection-rules","xai-colossus-memphis-gas-turbine-backup","google-kairos-power-fleet-agreement"],"sources":[{"label":"CBRE — North America Data Center Trends H2 2025","url":"https://www.cbre.com/insights/books/north-america-data-center-trends-h2-2025"},{"label":"PJM Interconnection — PJM Auction Procures 134,479 MW of Generation Resources","url":"https://www.pjm.com/-/media/DotCom/about-pjm/newsroom/2025-releases/20251217-pjm-auction-procures-134479-mw-of-generation-resources.pdf"},{"label":"GovTech — Georgia Approves New Rule to Charge Data Centers for Power","url":"https://www.govtech.com/products/georgia-approves-new-rule-to-charge-data-centers-for-power"},{"label":"American Action Forum — Virginia's New Data Center Electricity Rate Class","url":"https://www.americanactionforum.org/insight/virginias-new-data-center-electricity-rate-class/"},{"label":"TechCrunch — xAI is facing a lawsuit for operating over 400 MW of gas turbines without permits","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/18/xai-is-facing-a-lawsuit-for-operating-over-400-mw-of-gas-turbines-without-permits"},{"label":"Google — Google and Kairos Power sign agreement to advance new nuclear energy technology","url":"https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/sustainability/google-kairos-power-nuclear-energy-agreement/"},{"label":"Equinix investor release 2025-08-14","url":"https://investor.equinix.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1079/equinix-collaborates-with-leading-alternative-energy"},{"label":"ERCOT - Interconnection Process: Generation Entity Winter Weather Preparedness (30 Oct 2024)","url":"https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2024/10/30/0940-AM-ERCOT-Interconnection-Process-Generation-Entity-Winter-Weather-Preparedness-Fernandes.pdf"}]},{"id":"process-heat","name":"Factories and process heat","sector":"Manufacturing","incumbent":"A battery plant's special contract prices energy at $24.56/MWh plus a redacted demand charge at a 95% load factor; a remote pulp mill sells firm surplus power to its grid at $187/MWh; a chemical plant runs a self-owned 200 MW CHP fleet saving about $45M a year. Dow's Seadrift project buys steam and power from four 80 MWe units, the industrial template.","incumbent_low_mwh":25,"incumbent_high_mwh":187,"price_form":"Steam plus power to one host, host-owned or vendor-owned; the offtaker becomes the licensee if it owns the plant, which only a Dow-scale host can carry.","term":"20 years on the special contract; the Dow project has no published term.","clears":"optimized","verdict":"Grid-connected factories pay too little for any published estimate to beat. The sale exists only where heat is the product or the grid is remote, as at Corner Brook.","blocker":"One small host cannot carry a licensee's overhead; a 15 MWt block is pushed into a vendor-owned structure selling heat, for which no signed, priced precedent exists.","first_deal":"A remote mill or a plant retiring a 6–18 MW turbine block, where the reactor is a repowering option rather than a replacement for a depreciated CHP fleet.","benchmark_ids":["blueoval-sk-glendale-kentucky-utilities-special-contract","corner-brook-pulp-paper-nl-hydro-ppa","eastman-kingsport-chp","dow-x-energy-seadrift-xe-100-smr"],"sources":[{"label":"Kentucky Public Service Commission - Special Contract for Electric Service between Kentucky Utilities Company and BlueOval SK, LLC (Case No. 2023-00123)","url":"https://psc.ky.gov/pscecf/2023-00123/mike.hornung@lge-ku.com/04142023102139/07_-_KU-BOSK_Special_Contract_-_Contract_FINAL_-_REDACTED.pdf"},{"label":"Government of Newfoundland and Labrador - Newfoundland and Labrador Hydro Extends Power Purchase Agreement with Corner Brook Pulp and Paper","url":"https://www.gov.nl.ca/releases/2026/fin/0707n03/"},{"label":"U.S. DOE Southeast CHP Technical Assistance Partnership — Eastman's 200 MW CHP (Kingsport, TN) Project Profile","url":"https://chptap.ornl.gov/profile/67/eastman-Project_Profile.pdf"},{"label":"World Nuclear News - Dow's Seadrift site selected for X-energy SMR project","url":"https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/Articles/Dow-s-Seadrift-site-selected-for-X-energy-SMR-proj"}]}],"prospects":[{"id":"doyon-utilities","name":"Doyon Utilities (Fort Wainwright and Fort Greely, Alaska)","advantage":"sovereignty","sector":"Defense installations","region":"Interior Alaska","load":"Electric, heat, water and wastewater systems at Alaska Army installations; capacity not stated in the award record","documented":"An Alaska Native corporation joint venture holds a 51-year utility privatisation worth up to $3.08B, with $895M obligated since 2007, roughly $60M a year, and its generation is coal and oil delivered by rail and barge. Fort Wainwright is one of the nine Janus candidate installations and the only one whose displaced fuel is priced at Alaskan rates; it has not been matched to a vendor.","fit":"The reactor enters as an asset inside a rate base a regulator already approves, so it does not have to win a $/kW contest. The unit can be 5–20 MW because the plant it supplements is a central heat-and-power station.","sale_shape":"Rate-based generation inside the existing 10 U.S.C. 2688 contract, with the delivered-fuel line as the saving the contractor already prices.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"What is Doyon's delivered cost of coal and oil per MWh at Fort Wainwright, and does the privatisation contract allow new generation to be added to the rate base?","refs":[{"benchmark":"doyon-utilities-alaska-utility-privatization"},{"opportunity":"janus"},{"instrument":"dod-utilities-privatization-conveyance"}],"sources":[{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_SP060007C8263 (PIID SP0600-07-C-8263), Doyon Utilities LLC, Fort Wainwright AK","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_SP060007C8263_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"},{"label":"army.mil — Janus next steps","url":"https://www.army.mil/article/289074/army_announces_next_steps_on_janus_program_for_next_generation_nuclear_energy"},{"label":"10 U.S.C. 2688 — Utility systems: conveyance authority","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid%3AUSC-prelim-title10-section2688&num=0&edition=prelim"}]},{"id":"eielson-daf","name":"Department of the Air Force at Eielson (with Golden Valley Electric Association)","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Defense installations","region":"Fairbanks, Alaska","load":"Up to 5 MWe plus steam heat beside a 23 MW coal-fired plant that is 72 years old","documented":"A Notice of Intent to Award to Oklo for a 30-year firm-fixed-price power purchase agreement, contracted through DLA Energy, with the award to follow NRC licensing. No price has been published; the Air Force says it will settle the rate in negotiation.","fit":"The first commercial reactor contract on a domestic installation is written at exactly the microreactor scale, as a supplement to the base plant rather than a replacement.","sale_shape":"Owner-operator sells energy and heat under a long-term PPA to a central buying agency; the base's utility, GVEA, stays as supplier and backup.","status":"letter-of-intent","next_question":"What rate is DLA Energy prepared to pay, and does the environmental analysis open a path for a second vendor's unit at the same base?","refs":[{"benchmark":"eielson-afb-oklo-microreactor-noita"},{"site":"eielson-pilot"},{"opportunity":"eielson"}],"sources":[{"label":"Oklo Inc. - Oklo Selected as Intended Awardee to Provide Clean, Reliable Power to Eielson Air Force Base in Alaska","url":"https://oklo.com/newsroom/news-details/2025/Oklo-Selected-as-Intended-Awardee-to-Provide-Clean-Reliable-Power-to-Eielson-Air-Force-Base-in-Alaska/default.aspx"},{"label":"Alaska Public Media — 2023 selection + base power context","url":"https://alaskapublic.org/news/2023-09-07/contractor-selected-to-build-nuclear-power-plant-at-eielson-air-force-base"}]},{"id":"cvea","name":"Copper Valley Electric Association (Valdez and Glennallen)","advantage":"vendor-gap","sector":"Electric Utilities","region":"Alaska","load":"An islanded cooperative serving about 3,800 members; two 15 MWt units studied to replace the Valdez cogeneration unit","documented":"A completed pre-feasibility study found a micro modular reactor a match for the cooperative's needs, with cooperative ownership beating vendor ownership, year-round heat sales pivotal and federal tax credits worth 30–50% of capital. The board tabled the project indefinitely in August 2023, and the vendor, USNC, entered Chapter 11 in 2024. Alaska's SB 177 removed the legislative siting requirement in 2022.","fit":"The study, the site (a bedrock bench near the Trans-Alaska Pipeline) and the state law are all done. What is missing is a vendor with a licensable 5–15 MWe unit and heat offtake.","sale_shape":"Cooperative-owned unit in the rate base, with heat sold to a Valdez offtaker; the study says vendor ownership loses.","status":"orphaned","next_question":"Why did the board table it: cost, vendor risk or something else in the cached release? And is the cooperative open to re-running the study with a different vendor?","refs":[{"site":"cvea-valdez"}],"sources":[{"label":"CVEA × USNC — Pre-Feasibility Study (public version)","url":"https://www.cvea.org/assets/documents/pdfs/mmr/CVEA_Alaska_FS-RELEASEv01.pdf"},{"label":"CVEA — Potential MMR Project page (tabled status + document set)","url":"https://www.cvea.org/about/project-reports/potential-micro-modular-nuclear-reactor-project.html"}]},{"id":"src-saskatchewan","name":"Saskatchewan Research Council","advantage":"vendor-gap","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Saskatchewan, Canada","load":"Up to 5 MWe planned as a Crown-research-council-operated demonstration for northern and remote Saskatchewan","documented":"The first announced eVinci customer, with CA$80M of provincial funding and SRC as the licensed operator, lost its vendor when Westinghouse cancelled the contract in fall 2025 and moved eVinci to space, defence and government work. SRC says it is evaluating other microreactor technologies.","fit":"A government buyer with money committed, an operator licence plan and a stated northern use case, at the bottom of the band.","sale_shape":"Government-funded demonstration with a Crown operator; the vendor supplies the unit and fuel under Canadian export and CNSC review.","status":"orphaned","next_question":"Which vendors is SRC evaluating now, and is the CA$80M still appropriated?","refs":[{"opportunity":"canada-src"},{"site":"src-evinci"}],"sources":[{"label":"POWER — Westinghouse secures first eVinci customer","url":"https://www.powermag.com/westinghouse-secures-first-customer-for-evinci-nuclear-microreactor/"},{"label":"SRC — FAQs About Nuclear (cancellation of record)","url":"https://www.src.sk.ca/src-nuclear/additional-information"}]},{"id":"chalk-river-gfp","name":"Global First Power and Canadian Nuclear Laboratories, Chalk River","advantage":"vendor-gap","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Ontario, Canada","load":"Up to 45 MWt of process heat via molten salt at Canada's national laboratory campus","documented":"The first SMR licence application in Canada, filed in 2019 with a licence to prepare site and a federal environmental assessment, was paused by the regulator in 2024 when the parent vendor filed for bankruptcy. Ontario Power Generation is a co-venturer and the regulator's page still reads paused.","fit":"A national-laboratory host with the richest foreign filing trail in the class, and a co-venturing utility. The site work and the environmental record transfer to whichever vendor takes the venture.","sale_shape":"Process-heat demonstration at a federal lab campus; no provincial rate filing applies.","status":"orphaned","next_question":"Who owns the Global First Power venture after the bankruptcy sale, and will the CNSC application be transferred or withdrawn?","refs":[{"site":"chalk-river-mmr"}],"sources":[{"label":"CNSC — GFP MMR Project page (status of record)","url":"https://www.cnsc-ccsn.gc.ca/eng/reactors/new-reactor-power-plant-projects/new-reactor-power-plant-facilities/global-first-micro-modular-reactor-project/"},{"label":"CNSC — Regulatory review status for the MMR Project (archived)","url":"https://www.cnsc-ccsn.gc.ca/eng/reactors/research-reactors/other-reactor-facilities/regulatory-review-status-micro-modular-reactor/"}]},{"id":"red-dog","name":"Teck and NANA Regional Corporation, Red Dog mine","advantage":"off-grid-diesel","sector":"Mining","region":"Northwest Alaska","load":"About 25 MW, off-grid and diesel-only, burning roughly 14.6 million gallons a year; an 8.8 MW solar farm is expected to deliver about 2 MW in summer","documented":"The sharpest microreactor-shaped load in North America: one 20 MWe unit would replace the whole 24.5 MW diesel station. The landowner is an Alaska Native corporation, the power contractor is TUGLIQ, and the mine's closure is planned around 2032.","fit":"A single 20 MWe unit matches the load exactly; only a relocatable unit fits the remaining mine life.","sale_shape":"Third-party-owned generation behind the fence under a term contract, with the unit moving to the next site at closure.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"What does Teck pay per delivered gallon and per MWh today, and would NANA, as landowner, take an ownership stake in a relocatable unit?","refs":[{"benchmark":"red-dog-mine-solar-teck-nana-tugliq"}],"sources":[{"label":"ArcticToday - One of Alaska's flagship mines soon could draw energy from the sun","url":"https://www.arctictoday.com/one-of-alaskas-flagship-mines-soon-could-draw-energy-from-the-sun/"}]},{"id":"agnico-kivalliq","name":"Agnico Eagle and Nukik Corporation, Kivalliq region","advantage":"wires-constraint","sector":"Mining","region":"Nunavut, Canada","load":"The Meadowbank complex and Meliadine mine burn about 33.5 million litres of diesel a year, three-quarters of the 44.5 million litres the proposed line would displace","documented":"The competing supply is a C$3.2B, 1,200 km transmission line from Manitoba, revised up from C$1.2B, that does not arrive until 2032. The line is Inuit-owned through Nukik and also serves five communities on Qulliq's territory-wide diesel fleet at $555–1,130/MWh.","fit":"A handful of 20 MWe units would cover the mines' load for a fraction of the line's cost and years sooner. What they cannot buy is the community and ownership package that is mobilising the public money.","sale_shape":"Mine-anchored units sold through the line's own ownership structure, so the Inuit-owned corporation keeps the equity the wire would have given it.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Is Nukik open to a generation asset in place of or alongside the line, and what is Agnico's diesel contract price?","refs":[{"benchmark":"kivalliq-hydro-fibre-link-agnico-nukik"},{"benchmark":"qulliq-nunavut-interim-rates-2025"}],"sources":[{"label":"Nunatsiaq News - Kivalliq Hydro-Fibre Link estimated cost rises to $3.2B","url":"https://nunatsiaq.com/stories/article/kivalliq-hydro-fibre-link-estimated-cost-rises-to-3-2b/"},{"label":"Qulliq Energy Corporation - Interim Electricity Rates effective April 1, 2025 (General Rate Application)","url":"https://www.qec.nu.ca/interim-electricity-rates-effective-april-1-2025-general-rate-application"}]},{"id":"glencore-raglan","name":"Glencore, Raglan mine (with TUGLIQ Energy)","advantage":"off-grid-diesel","sector":"Mining","region":"Nunavik, Quebec","load":"An Arctic nickel mine burning about 60 million litres of diesel a year; two 3 MW wind turbines with flywheel, battery and hydrogen storage","documented":"The Government of Canada completion report for the Raglan pilot is where the $250–600/MWh industrial self-generation band comes from. The miner let a third party own the turbines and took federal money to de-risk the first unit. The same report says northern operators distrust new generation because a microgrid collapse at minus 40 stops mine ventilation.","fit":"A 5 MW unit at even $300/MWh clears the bottom of the band, and the third-party ownership precedent is already on this site.","sale_shape":"Developer-owned unit under a 20-year contract, the wind precedent's form, with the reactor proving it firms the microgrid.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"What is Raglan's current delivered diesel cost, and what firming test would the mine's electrical engineers require before trusting a reactor on the microgrid?","refs":[{"benchmark":"raglan-mine-wind-storage-tugliq-glencore"}],"sources":[{"label":"TUGLIQ Energy Co. / ecoENERGY Innovation Initiative - Glencore RAGLAN Mine Renewable Electricity Smart-Grid Pilot Demonstration, Public Completion Report GC 128296","url":"https://tugliq.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/2016-11-11-tugliq-raglan-public-report-en.pdf"},{"label":"Natural Resources Canada - Nunavik Mining: RAGLAN 2.0 Large Scale Renewable Energy Smart Grid","url":"https://natural-resources.canada.ca/funding-partnerships/nunavik-mining-raglan-20-large-scale-renewable-energy-smart-grid"}]},{"id":"qulliq-nunavut","name":"Qulliq Energy Corporation and the Government of Nunavut","advantage":"sovereignty","sector":"Electric Utilities","region":"Nunavut, Canada","load":"Territory-wide diesel generation; interim 2025 rates of $555–1,130/MWh by class","documented":"A territorial Crown utility that publishes the number a developer needs: a regulated retail rate two to four times any published microreactor estimate, on a fleet that is entirely diesel.","fit":"Even a 20-year levelised cost of $250–350/MWh undercuts every rate class by a factor of two. The constraints are community size, sealift logistics and the absence of a Canadian microreactor licence.","sale_shape":"Crown-utility-owned unit at a hub community, with the federal government as the capital partner it already is for the Kivalliq line.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Which Nunavut communities draw more than 1 MW year-round, and has the territory taken a position on nuclear under its own energy strategy?","refs":[{"benchmark":"qulliq-nunavut-interim-rates-2025"}],"sources":[{"label":"Qulliq Energy Corporation - Interim Electricity Rates effective April 1, 2025 (General Rate Application)","url":"https://www.qec.nu.ca/interim-electricity-rates-effective-april-1-2025-general-rate-application"},{"label":"Qulliq Energy Corporation - QEC's General Rate Application","url":"https://www.qec.nu.ca/qecs-general-rate-application"}]},{"id":"tanana-chiefs","name":"Tanana Chiefs Conference and the Alaska Village Electric Cooperative","advantage":"sovereignty","sector":"Electric Utilities","region":"Interior Alaska","load":"Eight village microgrids, each far below 1 MW, aggregated under a tribal energy-sovereignty award","documented":"A $32.6M DOE award, $26.1M federal, is retrofitting solar and storage into eight villages that run on diesel for 100% of their electricity, targeting a 40% cut. It creates an eight-village tribal power entity. A separate $5.0M award at Kokhanok buys about $5,000/kW of non-diesel capacity for a 170-person village.","fit":"No single village can take a 1 MWe unit; the aggregated tribal utility is the buyer that can, and it is the buyer the federal program just created.","sale_shape":"Tribal-utility-owned unit at a hub village with public capital, inside the PCE settlement.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Does any village in the eight, or a hub they connect to, draw over 1 MW, and is the tribal entity chartered to own generation?","refs":[{"benchmark":"tanana-chiefs-alaskan-tribal-energy-sovereignty-era"},{"benchmark":"kokhanok-paradigm-shift-era-microgrid"}],"sources":[{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_DECD0000069 (FAIN DECD0000069), Dena Nena Henash (Tanana Chiefs Conference), AK","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_DECD0000069_089/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_DECD0000120 (FAIN DECD0000120), Kokhanok Village, Lake and Peninsula AK","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_DECD0000120_089/"}]},{"id":"offgrid-ipps","name":"Off-grid mine power contractors (Zenith Energy, Aggreko, EDL, TUGLIQ)","advantage":"off-grid-diesel","sector":"Mining","region":"Australia, West Africa, Canadian North","load":"Hybrid stations of 35–95 MW where 20–40 MW of gas or diesel remains under a 60% renewable design","documented":"The contractors that own and run mine power hold the sites, the interconnections and the 10–16 year contracts: Zenith at Kathleen Valley (15 years, 27 MW gas plus 5 MW diesel residual), Aggreko at Syama (16 years, a 40% cost cut), EDL at Agnew (A$111.6M for about 35 MW), TUGLIQ at Raglan and Red Dog. One counterparty's risk was bridged by an A$25M export-credit guarantee.","fit":"The residual firm block under a renewable design is one 20 MWe unit per site, and the contractor is the party that would own and operate it behind the fence.","sale_shape":"The reactor vendor's channel is the contractor, not the miner: the contractor adds a reactor to a hybrid station it already runs under the existing term.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Which contractor has a portfolio site with 15 years of contract left and a 20 MW firm residual, and would an export-credit agency guarantee a first unit?","refs":[{"benchmark":"kathleen-valley-lithium-zenith-95mw-ppa"},{"benchmark":"syama-gold-mine-aggreko-16-year-psa"},{"benchmark":"agnew-gold-mine-hybrid-microgrid-edl"},{"benchmark":"essakane-solar-eren-iamgold-15-year-ppa"}],"sources":[{"label":"Zenith Energy - Liontown Resources signs Power Purchase Agreement with Zenith Energy","url":"https://zenithenergy.com.au/liontown-resources-signs-power-purchase-agreement-ppa-with-zenith-energy-for-the-largest-off-grid-renewable-energy-hybrid-power-station-in-australia/"},{"label":"Global Mining Review - Aggreko and Resolute sign hybrid power plant contract","url":"https://www.globalminingreview.com/exploration-development/17122019/aggreko-and-resolute-sign-hybrid-power-plant-contract/"},{"label":"ARENA - Agnew Renewable Energy Microgrid project record","url":"https://arena.gov.au/projects/agnew-renewable-energy-microgrid/"}]},{"id":"diamondback","name":"Diamondback Energy, Permian Basin","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Oil & Gas","region":"Midland, Texas","load":"50 MW across powerhouses for oilfield operations, under a 20-year PPA structure with a 20-year extension","documented":"A nonbinding letter of intent from April 2024 for Oklo to license, build, own and operate reactors supplying Diamondback's Permian operations. No site parcel, filing or binding conversion has been located.","fit":"An oilfield production hub draws tens of megawatts and a well pad a few, so the band fits the hub and a fleet of small units fits the field.","sale_shape":"Behind-the-fence supply to oilfield operations under a long-term PPA; no ERCOT or PUCT filing expected.","status":"letter-of-intent","next_question":"Has the letter of intent converted, and which hub is the first site?","refs":[{"site":"oklo-diamondback-permian"}],"sources":[{"label":"WNN — US companies sign up with Oklo for microreactor power","url":"https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/Articles/US-companies-sign-up-with-Oklo-for-microreactor-po"}]},{"id":"ianc","name":"Industrial Advanced Nuclear Consortium members","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Manufacturing","region":"Multi-site","load":"Remote well pads, offshore platforms, refinery and LNG heat, mining; technology-neutral across SMRs and microreactors","documented":"ExxonMobil, Shell, Chevron, ConocoPhillips, Rio Tinto, Freeport-McMoRan and Nucor formed a demand-aggregation consortium in September 2025 with a stated goal of making nuclear a viable industrial option by 2030. No member has issued a microreactor request for proposals, and one mining survey puts fewer than 10% of miners actively considering small reactors.","fit":"The consortium's use cases are the band's use cases, and it is the only place the industrial buyers have said so together.","sale_shape":"A pooled specification or a shared orderbook is what a consortium can sign that a single member cannot.","status":"consortium","next_question":"Will the consortium publish a common specification or a target price, and which member has a remote site with a 2028–2030 need?","refs":[{"opportunity":"ianc"}],"sources":[{"label":"The Open Group / IANC","url":"https://www.opengroup.org/IANC"},{"label":"BusinessWire — The Open Group launches IANC (2025-09-02)","url":"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250902229163/en/The-Open-Group-Launches-the-Industrial-Advanced-Nuclear-Consortium"}]},{"id":"equinix","name":"Equinix","advantage":"co-location","sector":"Compute","region":"Not site-assigned","load":"20 Kaleidos units of 1 MWe, committed with deposits; sites, schedule and unit price unpublished","documented":"The only signed microreactor purchase agreement in the commercial track, written as a fleet across sites named later. Colocation's asking rate of $196.25 per kW a month, about $269/MWh drawn continuously, is the all-in price a reactor block inside an Equinix campus competes with.","fit":"Fleet-shaped offtake only works with factory-built units, and twenty units under one owner share the staffing floor that a lone 1 MWe unit cannot carry.","sale_shape":"Purchase agreement with deposits, then per-site delivery under a resilience-block PPA against colocation and diesel economics.","status":"signed","next_question":"Which metros, under which state's retail-sale rule, and does each site sit under the local small-generator threshold?","refs":[{"opportunity":"equinix-radiant"},{"benchmark":"cbre-wholesale-colocation-pricing-h2-2025"},{"instrument":"reservation-fee-rofr-mfn-offtake"}],"sources":[{"label":"Equinix investor release 2025-08-14","url":"https://investor.equinix.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1079/equinix-collaborates-with-leading-alternative-energy"},{"label":"CBRE — North America Data Center Trends H2 2025","url":"https://www.cbre.com/insights/books/north-america-data-center-trends-h2-2025"}]},{"id":"hyperscalers","name":"Microsoft, Meta, Google, Amazon and Switch","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Compute","region":"United States","load":"Campuses of 50–500 MW and up, with a 1–20 MW dedicated block as the microreactor-shaped purchase","documented":"All five have signed nuclear instruments at scale: a 20-year restart PPA, a full-output PPA, a fleet agreement against an unlicensed vendor's roadmap, a phased four-unit development deal, a 12 GW non-binding master agreement and a prepayment that funds development directly. Each legal and sustainability team already owns a nuclear PPA playbook.","fit":"The precedent-clearing is done; a 1–20 MW resilience block rides on it procedurally. The block competes with the diesel fleet and colocation, and PJM's capacity price of about $121,700 per MW-year is the value the grid puts on firm capacity there.","sale_shape":"A resilience-block PPA or prepayment inside an existing framework, sized under the campus's own consumption so no power is sold.","status":"signed","next_question":"Which campus has a dedicated-block need in 2028–2030 that the utility cannot serve, and would the buyer accept a first unit under a fleet option?","refs":[{"benchmark":"microsoft-constellation-crane-clean-energy-center"},{"benchmark":"meta-constellation-clinton-clean-energy-center"},{"benchmark":"google-kairos-power-fleet-agreement"},{"benchmark":"amazon-energy-northwest-xe100-washington"},{"opportunity":"oklo-switch"},{"news":"meta-oklo-pike-county-2026-01-09"}],"sources":[{"label":"Constellation Energy — Constellation to Launch Crane Clean Energy Center","url":"https://www.constellationenergy.com/news/2024/Constellation-to-Launch-Crane-Clean-Energy-Center-Restoring-Jobs-and-Carbon-Free-Power-to-The-Grid.html"},{"label":"Constellation Energy — Constellation, Meta Sign 20-Year Deal for Clean, Reliable Nuclear Energy in Illinois","url":"https://www.constellationenergy.com/news/2025/constellation-meta-sign-20-year-deal-for-clean-reliable-nuclear-energy-in-illinois.html"},{"label":"Google — Google and Kairos Power sign agreement to advance new nuclear energy technology","url":"https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/sustainability/google-kairos-power-nuclear-energy-agreement/"},{"label":"X-energy — Amazon Invests in X-energy to Support Advanced Small Modular Nuclear Reactors and Expand Carbon-Free Power","url":"https://x-energy.com/news/amazon-invests-in-x-energy-to-support-advanced-small-modular-nuclear-reactors-and-expand-carbon-free-power/"},{"label":"Switch — Oklo and Switch form landmark strategic relationship","url":"https://www.switch.com/oklo-and-switch-form-landmark-strategic-relationship/"},{"label":"POWER — Meta Locks In Up to 6.6 GW of Nuclear Power Through Deals with Vistra, Oklo, and TerraPower","url":"https://www.powermag.com/meta-locks-in-up-to-6-6-gw-of-nuclear-power-through-deals-with-vistra-oklo-and-terrapower/"},{"label":"PJM Interconnection — PJM Auction Procures 134,479 MW of Generation Resources","url":"https://www.pjm.com/-/media/DotCom/about-pjm/newsroom/2025-releases/20251217-pjm-auction-procures-134479-mw-of-generation-resources.pdf"}]},{"id":"speed-constrained-ai","name":"Speed-constrained AI builders (xAI in Memphis, Valar and Nvidia in Utah, Aalo at RELLIS)","advantage":"speed-or-land","sector":"Compute","region":"Tennessee, Utah, Texas","load":"Hundreds of megawatts at xAI; a 30 MW announced data center in Utah; a reactor and a data center built together on a 2,400-acre university campus","documented":"xAI installed unpermitted gas turbines rather than wait for a utility connection, drawing over 1,700 public comments and lawsuits. Valar announced a 30 MW Utah data center with Nvidia after its test reactor reached criticality, with no contract, price or delivery date. Aalo filed for an early site permit at Texas A&M's RELLIS campus, which offers land to reactor developers.","fit":"The buyer's product is a delivery date. A microreactor's pitch is the permitting and community exposure gas turbines created, and a site where the land is already offered.","sale_shape":"Build the generation with the load on one site under one owner, with a delivery date and a curtailment position written as the terms.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"For each announced project, what is the executed contract, the delivery date and the price, and which regulator signs first?","refs":[{"benchmark":"xai-colossus-memphis-gas-turbine-backup"},{"news":"valar-nvidia-datacenter-2026-06-22"},{"site":"tamus-rellis"}],"sources":[{"label":"TechCrunch — xAI is facing a lawsuit for operating over 400 MW of gas turbines without permits","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/18/xai-is-facing-a-lawsuit-for-operating-over-400-mw-of-gas-turbines-without-permits"},{"label":"ANS/Nuclear Newswire — The deadline arrives: Checking in on the Reactor Pilot Program","url":"https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-02/article-8178/the-deadline-arrives-checking-in-on-the-reactor-pilot-program/"},{"label":"WNN — Four SMR developers aim to build at Texas A&M site","url":"https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/four-smr-developers-aim-to-build-reactors-at-texas-am-university-site"}]},{"id":"ercot-large-loads","name":"Texas large loads under Senate Bill 6 (and Last Energy's Haskell County site)","advantage":"speed-or-land","sector":"Compute","region":"Texas","load":"New loads of 75 MW and up must accept curtailment or run their own backup; a 200-acre site holds thirty planned 20 MWe units for data-center supply","documented":"SB6 makes a large Texas load a grid-management liability with a $100,000 minimum study fee and mandatory backup disclosure. ERCOT's small-generation process handles a unit under 10 MW in 8–12 months against 18–30 for large generation. Last Energy has secured land for thirty units and filed for an ERCOT connection, with no named offtaker.","fit":"Firm, non-curtailable on-site generation is worth more under SB6, and 9.9 MW units fit the fast process by rule.","sale_shape":"Behind-the-meter blocks under the 10 MW threshold at loads that would otherwise accept curtailment.","status":"policy-gated","next_question":"Which large loads have filed backup-disclosure under SB6 with diesel, and which would substitute a reactor block for it?","refs":[{"benchmark":"ercot-sb6-large-load-interconnection-rules"},{"site":"lastenergy-haskell"},{"instrument":"ercot-connect-and-manage-small-generation"}],"sources":[{"label":"McGuireWoods — Texas Senate Bill 6 Significantly Expands Regulatory Oversight Over Large Loads in ERCOT","url":"https://www.mcguirewoods.com/client-resources/alerts/2025/7/texas-senate-bill-6-significantly-expands-regulatory-oversight-over-large-loads-in-ercot/"},{"label":"WNN — Last Energy plans Texan microreactor plant","url":"https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/last-energy-plans-texan-microreactor-plant"},{"label":"ERCOT - Interconnection Process: Generation Entity Winter Weather Preparedness (30 Oct 2024)","url":"https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2024/10/30/0940-AM-ERCOT-Interconnection-Process-Generation-Entity-Winter-Weather-Preparedness-Fernandes.pdf"}]},{"id":"clean-ports","name":"Port of Los Angeles and the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey","advantage":"wires-constraint","sector":"Transportation","region":"California, New York and New Jersey","load":"Battery-electric cargo equipment, chargers, shore power and 143 MWh of batteries at Los Angeles alone: a multi-tens-of-megawatt peak set by ship calls","documented":"Over $1.4B of federal and matching Clean Ports money at two ports converts diesel machinery into electrical load by 2028 and funds no supply. The whole gap falls on two urban distribution utilities. Ports already accept $7.0M per container berth and $14.7M per cruise berth for shore-power connections.","fit":"The reactor competes with a feeder upgrade and demand charges, not a $/MWh tariff, at a site where a 5–20 MW base load now exists.","sale_shape":"Supply for the electrified terminal under an energy-as-a-service structure, with shore power as the seasonal add.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"What has LADWP or PSE&G quoted the port for the distribution upgrade, and on what schedule?","refs":[{"benchmark":"port-of-los-angeles-epa-clean-ports"},{"benchmark":"port-authority-ny-nj-epa-clean-ports"},{"benchmark":"carb-at-berth-shore-power-capex"}],"sources":[{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_97T27601 (FAIN 97T27601), City of Los Angeles, Clean Ports Program","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_97T27601_068/"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Assistance award ASST_NON_96275025 (FAIN 96275025), Port Authority of New York & New Jersey, Clean Ports Program","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/ASST_NON_96275025_068/"},{"label":"California Dept of Finance / CARB - Standardized Regulatory Impact Assessment, Ocean-Going Vessels At Berth (per-berth capex)","url":"https://dof.ca.gov/media/docs/forecasting/economics/major-regulations/major-regulations-table/SRIA_with_Appendices-Proposed_Control_Measure_for_Ocean-Going_Vessels_At_Berth-080119.pdf"},{"label":"Port of Seattle - The Past, Present, and Future of Shore Power","url":"https://www.portseattle.org/blog/past-present-and-future-shore-power"}]},{"id":"dp-world","name":"DP World, Thames Freeport","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Transportation","region":"United Kingdom","load":"One 20 MWe unit for a freeport, target online 2030","documented":"The one commercial port operator anywhere with a named microreactor deal, under UK regulatory review since a preliminary design review in July 2025. It is a competitor's deployment, and proof that a port will sign.","fit":"A freeport's terminal load is inside the band, and a UK site answers to the Office for Nuclear Regulation plus US export control, not the NRC.","sale_shape":"Named commercial customer with the vendor carrying the regulatory review.","status":"signed","next_question":"What did DP World agree to pay, and does the freeport's grid connection or its own load justify the 20 MW?","refs":[{"opportunity":"uk-lastenergy"}],"sources":[{"label":"The Civil Engineer — UK/US partnership fast-tracks SMRs and microreactors (Last Energy PWR-20 / Thames Freeport)","url":"https://www.thecivilengineer.org/news/fast-track-nuclear-how-the-ukus-partnership-accelerates-smrs-and-microreactors"}]},{"id":"healthcare-resilience","name":"Healthcare hosts and their resilience developers (Loma Linda, NextNRG, Kaiser Permanente)","advantage":"co-location","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Southern California","load":"Clinics and hospitals averaging 1.7 MW to single-digit megawatts, with a 6–10 hour battery as the current resilience product","documented":"Healthcare hosts are signing 28–30 year behind-the-meter contracts at 15 to 25 cents/kWh with no host capital. The largest hospital renewable microgrid in the country buys ten hours of ride-through. CMS's categorical waiver lets something other than a generator be an emergency source, while the ten-second start rule keeps a battery or engine in front.","fit":"A 1–5 MW unit is the drop-in for the certified fuel-cell block at these sites, and the willingness to pay is documented at the top of the mass-produced band.","sale_shape":"Resilience service plus energy under an energy-services agreement, generators retained, sold through the developers who already hold the contracts.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Which developer's portfolio has hosts whose FEMA benefit-cost worksheets exceed $50M, and will the state authority accept a reactor as part of the microgrid?","refs":[{"benchmark":"loma-linda-faculty-medical-clinics-ppa"},{"benchmark":"nextnrg-sunnyside-topanga-microgrid-ppas"},{"benchmark":"kaiser-ontario-medical-center-microgrid"},{"instrument":"cms-health-care-microgrid-categorical-waiver"}],"sources":[{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge — University Healthcare Clinic Powers Up Microgrid with On-Site Solar and Tesla Battery in California","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/microgrids/critical-services/news/55312608/university-healthcare-clinic-powers-up-microgrid-with-on-site-solar-and-tesla-battery-in-california"},{"label":"Microgrid Knowledge — Two California Healthcare Facilities Choose Long-Term Microgrid PPAs with New Developer","url":"https://www.microgridknowledge.com/commercial-microgrids/news/55303895/two-california"},{"label":"PR Newswire / Kaiser Permanente — Kaiser Permanente Debuts Largest Hospital-based Renewable Microgrid in U.S.","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/kaiser-permanente-debuts-largest-hospital-based-renewable-microgrid-in-us-302431273.html"},{"label":"Brach Eichler — CMS Issues Categorical Waiver for Microgrid Systems as Alternate Power Sources in Health Care Facilities","url":"https://www.bracheichler.com/insights/cms-issues-categorical-waiver-for-microgrid-systems-as-alternate-power-sources-in-health-care-facilities-2/"}]},{"id":"water-utilities","name":"Water utilities with a FEMA benefit-cost record (WaterOne, PRASA)","advantage":"co-location","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Kansas and Puerto Rico","load":"Regional water treatment and pumping systems of 1–10 MW that must run through a grid outage","documented":"FEMA scored WaterOne's $6.5M generator project at a 38.09 benefit-cost ratio with $261M of net benefits, and pays the whole $16.5M of PRASA's generators in Toa Alta against $150.8M of modeled benefits. The generator's fuel has to keep arriving during the storm that took the grid down.","fit":"A 1–10 MW unit matches the load, sells energy every hour instead of idling, and the federal worksheet already prices the outage exposure.","sale_shape":"Firm-power asset in the tens of millions argued from the FEMA worksheet, with the diesel fleet kept as secondary backup.","status":"evidence-only","next_question":"Which water utilities hold a FEMA worksheet above $100M of net benefits and a load above 1 MW?","refs":[{"benchmark":"waterone-johnson-county-fema-generators"},{"benchmark":"prasa-toa-alta-fema-generators"}],"sources":[{"label":"FEMA OpenFEMA API — Hazard Mitigation Assistance Projects v4, project LPDM-PJ-07-KS-2022-001 (WaterOne, Johnson County KS)","url":"https://www.fema.gov/api/open/v4/HazardMitigationAssistanceProjects?$filter=projectIdentifier%20eq%20%27LPDM-PJ-07-KS-2022-001%27"},{"label":"FEMA OpenFEMA API — Hazard Mitigation Assistance Projects v4, project DR-4339-0019-R (Puerto Rico Aqueduct and Sewer Authority, Toa Alta)","url":"https://www.fema.gov/api/open/v4/HazardMitigationAssistanceProjects?$filter=projectIdentifier%20eq%20%27DR-4339-0019-R%27"}]},{"id":"university-hosts","name":"Universities with a licensing track (Penn State, Texas A&M, Illinois, Abilene Christian)","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Pennsylvania, Texas, Illinois","load":"Research reactors of 1–45 MWt on campus, with district heat and steam integration as the use case","documented":"Four universities hold real filings: Abilene Christian has a construction permit issued in 2024, Illinois has a construction permit application for a 45 MWt unit, Penn State filed intent for a 15 MWt eVinci-based reactor, and Texas A&M holds an early-site-permit track on a 2,400-acre campus with four vendor site agreements.","fit":"The nonprofit research-reactor pathway is a different door from a commercial licence, and a campus is a single owner whose load absorbs the output.","sale_shape":"Research reactor on a campus with heat integration; the university is the licensee and the vendor supplies the unit.","status":"selected","next_question":"Which of the four will fuel first, and does any campus intend to take power or heat commercially rather than as research?","refs":[{"site":"psu-frontier"},{"site":"tamus-rellis"},{"site":"uiuc-kronos"},{"site":"acu-msrr"}],"sources":[{"label":"NRC ADAMS — Penn State notice of intent, ML25059A029","url":"https://www.nrc.gov/docs/ML2505/ML25059A029.pdf"},{"label":"WNN — Four SMR developers aim to build at Texas A&M site","url":"https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/four-smr-developers-aim-to-build-reactors-at-texas-am-university-site"},{"label":"UIUC NPRE — Illinois Microreactor Project page","url":"https://npre.illinois.edu/about/illinois-microreactor-project"},{"label":"NRC — News release 24-071: construction permit issued for ACU research reactor","url":"https://www.nrc.gov/docs/ML2427/ML24276A165.pdf"}]},{"id":"privatized-base-utilities","name":"Privatised base utilities (Sandhills Utility at Fort Bragg, City Light and Power at Fort Campbell)","advantage":"nuclear-interest","sector":"Defense installations","region":"North Carolina, Kentucky","load":"The electrical distribution systems of Janus installations, owned and operated under DLA Energy privatisation awards","documented":"Sandhills Utility owns and operates Fort Bragg's distribution system; City Light and Power has run Fort Campbell's since 2018. Neither source names a Janus utility partner, and the Aberdeen award shows the buyer of on-base generation is increasingly the privatised utility signing $24–34M microgrid contracts at four installations at once. Janus converts to an Army power purchase agreement after the first year.","fit":"The reactor connects to wires these companies own, so they are the interconnection counterparty and the likely tariff partner when Janus becomes a PPA.","sale_shape":"Interconnection and tariff terms with the privatised utility, then the Army PPA.","status":"selected","next_question":"What do the privatisation contracts say about third-party generation on the base, and who pays for the interconnection?","refs":[{"site":"janus-bragg"},{"site":"janus-campbell"},{"benchmark":"aberdeen-proving-ground-microgrid-backup-power"}],"sources":[{"label":"POWER — The Janus Five: 20+ Commercial Nuclear Microreactors, Starting in 2028","url":"https://www.powermag.com/the-janus-five-20-commercial-nuclear-microreactors-starting-in-2028/","status":"snippet-only"},{"label":"USAspending.gov API — Award CONT_AWD_W912QR25CA034 (PIID W912QR25CA034), City Light & Power Aberdeen LLC","url":"https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/awards/CONT_AWD_W912QR25CA034_9700_-NONE-_-NONE-/"}]},{"id":"texas-programs","name":"Texas Energy Fund backup program and the HB 14 nuclear fund","advantage":"speed-or-land","sector":"Civic Infrastructure","region":"Texas","load":"Site-scale backup at hospitals, water treatment, nursing homes and police and fire stations under a $1.8B program; a $350M nuclear fund with few eligible projects","documented":"The backup power program buys the replacement outright from a technology list that does not name nuclear. The state's nuclear fund opened in 2026 with zero eligible microreactor projects, and the one Texas microreactor project with an NRC docket is excluded by a rule.","fit":"Both programs are sized for the band and both are closed to it by a list, which is a policy change away.","sale_shape":"Substitution into live procurement once the technology list includes reactors, with the fund as the capital partner.","status":"policy-gated","next_question":"What rulemaking adds a reactor to the backup-power technology list, and what is the eligibility rule the HB 14 fund applies?","refs":[{"opportunity":"texas-backup"},{"instrument":"texas-backup-power-package-program"},{"news":"taneo-fund-opens-2026-04-01"}],"sources":[{"label":"University of Houston Energy Innovation — Texas backup power microgrid resilience (2025)","url":"https://www.uh.edu/uh-energy-innovation/news-events/energy/stories/2025/microgirdresilience.php"},{"label":"Texas Solar Energy Society — Power When It Matters Most: Texas' Backup Power Package Program","url":"https://txses.org/power-when-it-matters-most-texas-backup-power-package-program/"},{"label":"ANS/Nuclear Newswire — Texas opens $350M in nuclear funding","url":"https://www.ans.org/news/2026-04-09/article-7920/texas-opens-350m-in-nuclear-funding/"}]},{"id":"fuel-chokepoints","name":"BWXT, Standard Nuclear and Centrus","advantage":"supply-chain","sector":"Supply chain","region":"Virginia, Tennessee, Ohio","load":"TRISO fabrication for every Janus vendor and the only domestic HALEU cascade","documented":"BWXT makes the TRISO fuel it uses at Fort Campbell and supplies its Janus competitors from Lynchburg. Standard Nuclear holds Radiant's multi-ton agreement through 2031 and Antares' one-ton deal with options through 2035, and priced a downsized IPO in July 2026. Centrus signed a $900M fixed-price contract to move its Piketon cascade to commercial production. The GAO says nobody yet knows how much HALEU defence microreactors will need.","fit":"Fuel does not get cheaper with volume and no HALEU price is published, so the fuel partner sets the one cost line a vendor cannot learn down.","sale_shape":"Multi-year fabrication agreements with options, ahead of any unit order; a merchant fuel supplier to the whole class is a better business than one reactor.","status":"signed","next_question":"What does a ton of fabricated TRISO cost, and which vendor's allocation covers its unit count?","refs":[{"news":"army-janus-bwxt-fort-campbell-2026-08-26"},{"news":"radiant-standard-nuclear-triso-2026-08-20"},{"news":"standard-nuclear-ipo-downsized-2026-07-15"},{"news":"centrus-900m-contract-signed-2026-06-30"},{"news":"gao-haleu-demand-skepticism-2026-08-25"}],"sources":[{"label":"POWER — The Janus Five: 20+ Commercial Nuclear Microreactors, Starting in 2028","url":"https://www.powermag.com/the-janus-five-20-commercial-nuclear-microreactors-starting-in-2028/"},{"label":"Renaissance Capital — Small modular reactor fuel developer Standard Nuclear prices previously downsized IPO at $15","url":"https://www.renaissancecapital.com/IPO-Center/News/120497/Small-modular-reactor-fuel-developer-Standard-Nuclear-prices-previously-dow"},{"label":"POWER — Centrus Signs $900M DOE Contract, Pivots Sole U.S. HALEU Cascade to Commercial Operation","url":"https://www.powermag.com/centrus-signs-900m-doe-contract-pivots-sole-u-s-haleu-cascade-to-commercial-operation/"},{"label":"ANS/Nuclear Newswire — GAO report analyzes nuclear fuel efforts in national security and commercial sectors","url":"https://www.ans.org/news/2026-08-25/article-8336/gao-report-analyzes-nuclear-fuel-efforts-in-national-security-and-commercial-sectors/"}]}]};window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('mr:strategy'));
